---
title: Data-driven requests
intent: Run one request for each row of a checked-in CSV file.
group: core
features:
- data-driven
command: curlew run examples/cookbook/data-driven.yaml --var mud="$MUDFLAT_URL" --var ws="$MUDFLAT_WS_URL" --var run="$RUN_ID"
order: 20
runnable: true
---

The sibling `data.csv` contains two rows. Paths are resolved relative to the collection. Each row supplies name and role variables; the two iterations must pass. This local echo example does not provision real users.

## Prerequisites

Use the complete repository checkout and start Mudflat as described in the [cookbook setup](https://github.com/weiqigod/curlew/blob/main/site/README.md). Run these commands from the repository root with `curlew` on PATH.

```bash
export MUDFLAT_URL="${MUDFLAT_URL:-http://127.0.0.1:18080}"
export MUDFLAT_WS_URL="${MUDFLAT_WS_URL:-ws://127.0.0.1:18080}"
export RUN_ID="cookbook-$(date +%s)-$$"
```

## Run it

```bash
curlew run examples/cookbook/data-driven.yaml --var mud="$MUDFLAT_URL" --var ws="$MUDFLAT_WS_URL" --var run="$RUN_ID"
```

A successful execution exits 0. Read assertion outcomes as well as the exit code.
No example output or timing numbers are fabricated here.

## Complete collection

<!-- cookbook-source: examples/cookbook/data-driven.yaml -->
```yaml
name: Data-driven echo
requests:
  - name: Echo row
    data_driven:
      source: data.csv
    request:
      method: POST
      url: "{{mud}}/echo"
      body:
        name: "{{name}}"
        role: "{{role}}"
    assertions:
      status: 200
      body:
        $.request.body_len: { greater_than: 0 }
```
